# Per-VM vanity host list: copy to deploy/tenants.caddy (gitignored; deploy.sh
# does this automatically if the file is missing) and add one block per
# customer vanity host (docs/founder-runbooks/custom-domain-provisioning.md
# § 3a). The host also needs the customer's DNS record pointing at this VM.
#
# Platform hosts (<slug>.<APP_DOMAIN>) do NOT go here. Since docs/decisions.md
# §364 they are served by CloudFront's wildcard, add-tenant.sh writes nothing
# here, and deploy.sh removes any platform block it finds.
#
# After editing, apply without downtime:
#   ./compose.sh exec caddy caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
# Caddy mounts this single file, so the container keeps the inode it started
# with: an editor that saves by writing a new file and renaming it over this one
# leaves Caddy reading the old list and the reload silently changes nothing. Edit
# in place, or recreate instead: ./compose.sh up -d --no-deps --force-recreate caddy
# (deploy.sh checks for this itself).
#
# Example: the acme tenant's vanity host.
#
# acme.acmecorp.com {
# 	import vanity
# }
